## Guide Audit Follow-Up

The final customization audit found typed minor ticks and the native domainLine option were omitted by the TypeScript renderer. The execution lane reproduced 12 mismatches in the registered quick render suite before its fix (51/63 passed, zero harness errors). Seventeen additional neutral cases cover side orientation, default/custom subdivision and size, explicit overrides, single-major behavior, grids, logarithmic mapped-position interpolation, scale-range bounds and domain aliases. The existing scene census and band-axis expectations now reflect the native domain-line default. Registered exhaustive inference passed425/425 and strict build passed248 exports after the guide changes. Actual native measurement passed six minor positions and stock/custom graph name order,37 transform comparisons and137 layout comparisons in a focused compiler diagnostic. The combined native target is still required.

## Authored Unknown-Scale Follow-Up

An actual comparison of admitted linear options `{unknown:-5}` against independent d3-scale `.unknown(-5)` reproduced null mapping to0 instead of-5 and undefined/NaN/nonnumeric text mapping toNaN instead of-5. Native scale keys do not yet admit unknown, although canonical Rust forwards the authored option. Both execution lanes are fixing this supported option and default missing-position gaps under existing inference/scale ownership. Final scale and full native replay remain pending.

The independent missing-input baseline executed105 checks:49 passed,33 mismatches and23 exceptions, including invalid-input color interpolation. D3 direct diverging scales coerce null to zero even with an unknown override; continuous/sequential scales use fallback. Quantize/threshold nonnumeric strings select the first bucket while quantile uses fallback. The implementation lanes are preserving these observed per-family semantics, with separate positional-gap behavior for absent authored data. Native null, empty-string and boolean cells are now distinguished through first-party data tokens rather than a shared empty scalar encoding; new typed-row/compiler and native mutation fixtures are pending final execution.

